// --- the cast: named characters with a fixed sheet ---------------------------
// A character sheet is one block of text — the **name first**, then the canonical
// description that must not drift between stills: age, build, skin, hair, eyes,
// marks, wardrobe. The name is the token that keeps the model pointed at the
// same person, and the sheet is what keeps her the same person.
//
// `character` stands in for `subject`, `age`, `physique` and `skin` (see
// `replaces` in src/config.js): while a character is set, those dimensions are
// left out of the prompt entirely, and `expression` stays free so the face can
// change shot to shot. Remove the character chip and the generic actor
// dimensions are rolled again.
//
// More characters can be loaded at runtime from a sheet URL (the "Character
// sheet URL" control) without touching this file: JSON, or one plain
// `Name: description, description` line per character. A loaded character with
// the same name overrides the one here.
