// --- pose or action ----------------------------------------------------------
// `pose` and `action` answer two halves of one question — where the bodies are,
// and what they are doing there — and rolling both lets them contradict each
// other (doggy style fighting a blowjob). Perchance's own alternation settles it
// without any code: one branch is picked per roll, and the block inside the
// winning branch is what gets evaluated:
//
//   {[root.pose.selectOne.evaluateItem]|[root.action.selectOne.evaluateItem]}
//
// Odds work as everywhere else, so `^3` on a branch makes it three times as
// likely, and a third branch can offer both at once when a shot really wants
// them:
//
//   {[root.pose.selectOne.evaluateItem]|[root.action.selectOne.evaluateItem]|[root.pose.selectOne.evaluateItem], [root.action.selectOne.evaluateItem]}
//
// `pose` and `action` stay whole lists underneath: either can be switched on as
// its own dimension by adding it back to `idea.parts`, for a shot that needs to
// pin the position and roll the act (or the other way round).
act
  {[root.pose.selectOne.evaluateItem]|[root.action.selectOne.evaluateItem]}

