// The negative is deliberately ONE line. It is a chain of comma-separated
// terms, and several terms carry commas *inside* a parenthesised weight group
// ("(classical Greek, Hellenistic, Roman:1.4)", "((watermark, ((text)),
// signature, logo, low quality,))"), plus one pair with no separator at all
// ("missing arms(low quality, worst quality, normal quality:1.2)"). Split onto
// fragment lines, `joinFragments` would insert a ", " at every break and quietly
// corrupt those groups ("low quality, ))", "missing arms, (low quality"). One
// line round-trips the text byte-for-byte, and it needs no `$output` because it
// has no children. Perchance reads `[`, `{` and `^` as syntax; this text has
// none of them, so it stays plain.
//
// NOTE: this block still contains "close up" among the quality terms, while the
// `shot` list offers "close-up" and "extreme close-up". The two pull against
// each other — kept as written, because it is the user's own negative prompt.
